Subject: [cuentapepas] YOLOX Trainer: store AP values as float in checkpoints

COCOeval returns numpy.float64, which torch.load(weights_only=True) - the default since torch 2.6
and what YOLOX --resume uses - refuses to unpickle. Plain floats keep resume and export loading safe.
Applied by tools/setup-yolox.sh.
---
diff --git a/yolox/core/trainer.py b/yolox/core/trainer.py
index 8f8016e..f36f689 100644
--- a/yolox/core/trainer.py
+++ b/yolox/core/trainer.py
@@ -404,8 +404,10 @@ class Trainer:
                 "start_epoch": self.epoch + 1,
                 "model": save_model.state_dict(),
                 "optimizer": self.optimizer.state_dict(),
-                "best_ap": self.best_ap,
-                "curr_ap": ap,
+                # cuentapepas patch: COCOeval returns numpy.float64; plain floats keep the checkpoint
+                # loadable with torch.load(weights_only=True), the default since torch 2.6 (used by --resume).
+                "best_ap": float(self.best_ap),
+                "curr_ap": None if ap is None else float(ap),
             }
             save_checkpoint(
                 ckpt_state,
